Confirmed: Riverpod forbids modifying other providers during a provider build. Fix: defer the handler body to a microtask. Use `Future<void>.microtask(...)` or `scheduleMicrotask`.

Implementation:

```dart
void _handleUnauthorized() {
  if (!mounted) return;
  _api.clearToken();
  Future<void>.microtask(() {
    if (!mounted) return;
    ref.read(sessionNoticeProvider.notifier).set('Your session expired. Log in again.');
    ref.read(sessionUserIdProvider.notifier).set(null);
    ref.read(sessionRefreshProvider).ping();
  });
}
```

But `clearToken()` during build is fine (plain field). The state changes happen after.

However: multiple concurrent 401s schedule multiple microtasks; idempotent, fine.

Will the test's `settle` run microtasks? `tester.pump` flushes microtasks. Yes.

Also: when the provider fetch continues after handler returns, it throws StateError ÔåÆ stream error "Invalid or expired token." Then session clears in microtask; provider rebuilds to empty list. Fine.

Remove debug prints and try/catch now, implement microtask.

Also remove fake print.

