Now widget tests. Add to tasks_tab_test.dart:

Test 1: bulk complete via long-press.
```dart
testWidgets('long-press selects tasks and bulk completes them', (tester) async {
  final fixture = Fixture();
  for (var i = 1; i <= 2; i++) {
    fixture.api.addTask(Task(id: i, title: 'Bulk $i', projectId: fixture.project.id, createdAt: DateTime.now()));
  }
  await pumpTaskPlanner(... user);
  await _openTasks(tester);

  await tester.longPress(find.text('Bulk 1'));
  await settle(tester);
  expect(find.text('1 selected'), findsOneWidget);

  await tester.tap(find.text('Bulk 2'));
  await settle(tester);
  expect(find.text('2 selected'), findsOneWidget);

  await tester.tap(find.byTooltip('Complete selected'));
  await settle(tester);
  expect(find.text('2 completed'), findsOneWidget);
  expect(fixture.api.tasks.every((t) => t.status == 'completed'), isTrue);
});
```

Note longPress on `find.text('Bulk 1')` ÔÇö the long press hits the text inside the tile; the outer GestureDetector should receive it. But InkWell may win the arena for long press? InkWell only has onTap; gesture arena: long press recognizer from outer GestureDetector, tap recognizer from InkWell. Long press wins after timeout. Should work.

Test 2: bulk reassign.
```dart
testWidgets('bulk reassign selects an assignee and applies it', (tester) async {
  final fixture = Fixture();
  ... two tasks
  open tasks; longPress Bulk 1; tap Bulk 2;
  await tester.tap(find.byTooltip('Reassign selected'));
  await settle(tester);
  expect(find.text('Reassign selected tasks'), findsOneWidget);
  // Reassign disabled until a member is chosen
  final button = find.widgetWithText(FilledButton, 'Reassign');
  expect(tester.widget<FilledButton>(button).onPressed, isNull);
  await tester.tap(find.text('Olive Owner'));  // member list includes active accounts of project
  await settle(tester);
  await tester.tap(button);
  await settle(tester);
  expect(find.text('2 reassigned'), findsOneWidget);
  expect(fixture.api.tasks.every((t) => t.assigneeId == fixture.owner.id), isTrue);
});
```

The dialog lists all project members: fixture has owner (Olive), user (Bob), pending Carol? `_membersFor` uses visibleMembersProvider which likely includes active + pending? It filters by project; pending may be included. Bob and Olive. Choose 'Olive Owner'. But the member name might appear elsewhere (task assignee labels). In the dialog, `find.text('Olive Owner')` unique enough? The tiles' assignee labels currently "Whole project". So unique.

Also, does `visibleMembersProvider` load for a regular user? Members tab visible for all; provider fetches `/members` (scoped). FakeApiClient handles. Should include fixture accounts of project 1 (owner, user, pending). Fine.

Test 3: leave batch? Also test that a plain tap still opens the editor (existing tests?). E11-like "editing a task persists subtask completion" already taps title to open ÔÇö with the refactor, onTap moves to TaskTile (innermost). Works.

Run tests after adding.

Then rebuild web & test E14.

Let me add the tests.

