Now add the widget test to home_screen_test. Note pumpApp uses `api.me = account`. For the role change test:

```dart
testWidgets('account changes made elsewhere refresh when the app resumes', (tester) async {
  await pumpApp(tester, user);
  expect(find.byType(NavigationDestination), findsNWidgets(5));

  // Admin changed Bob to viewer while the app was backgrounded.
  api.me = Account(... role: 'viewer' ...);
  tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.paused);
  tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.resumed);
  await tester.pump();
  await tester.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 400));

  expect(find.byType(NavigationDestination), findsNWidgets(3));
  expect(find.text('Planner'), findsNothing);
  expect(find.text('Dashboard'), findsNothing);
});
```

Need to ensure routing index stays valid. HomeScreen guards index. Good.

Does `handleAppLifecycleStateChanged` exist as method on TestWidgetsFlutterBinding? Yes, `tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.resumed)` is a method on ServicesBinding (in newer Flutter, `TestWidgetsFlutterBinding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged`). Alternatively `tester.binding.defaultBinaryMessenger.handlePlatformMessage('flutter/lifecycle', ...)`. Let's try the method.

Also DataSync ping triggers all watchFromApi streams, including members and tasks, causing some pending timers. Pumps should resolve.

Add test after "admin has no personal Mine tab".

