content.text:
Note `fixture.api..me = viewer` ÔÇö cascade assignment syntax `..me = viewer` works? Cascades can assign fields: `obj..me = viewer;` yes.

But `expect(() => future, throwsStateError)` with async function returning a Future: the closure returns Future, matcher `throwsStateError` on a function returning a Future ÔÇö need `expect(fixture.api.post(...), throwsStateError)` (non-closure) or `expect(() async => ..., throwsA(...))`. Simpler: `await expectLater(fixture.api.post(...), throwsStateError);`. Add `async` to testWidgets (already async). Let me fix.

Also, viewer mutations in fake aren't enforced yet ÔÇö need `_requireCanMutate` in `_createTask`, `_updateTask`, `_completeTask`, `_reopenTask`, delete, bulk, member create/confirm. Implement.

But careful: `_createTask` is also used by admin/owner. Viewer test asserts throws.

Let me add `_requireCanMutate()`:

```dart
void _requireCanMutate() {
  if (_requireSignedIn().role == 'viewer') {
    throw StateError('A viewer cannot change data.');
  }
}
```

Apply at start of `_createTask`, `_updateTask`, `_completeTask`, `_reopenTask`, delete task/subtask, subtask create/patch/delete, bulk, `_createMember`, `_confirmMember`, archive/restore (admin-only already, but viewer isn't admin so ok), role (admin-only).

Actually `_updateTask` used by bulk reassign; fine.

Also need test of `post('/tasks')` fake requires `_createTask` which calls `_requireSignedIn`; viewer -> throws. Good.

Change viewer test to expectLater with Future.

