The app is logged in as **Bob**, not Alice! E16's login logic: reload, pageText; if `/Log in/` no; `else if (!/Alice/.test(text))`... but `pageText` includes "Alice" somewhere (member names in tasks, e.g. tasks assigned to Alice / "Assigned member"?). Indeed pageText contains roster names, so `!/Alice/` was false ÔåÆ it kept Bob. Then clicking Planner as Bob works (Planner visible), but waitForText('Search tasks') failed? Bob is a user ÔåÆ planner body non-admin; search should show. But body after manual click shows Planner with sections, **no "Search tasks"** text in body innerText! The hint text isn't in body innerText? In Flutter, hintText may not render into semantics text until? Hmm, the `TextField` hint is visible; semantics might expose it as placeholder but not textContent. So `waitForText('Search tasks')` may fail because the hint is only in the input's placeholder (DOM), not pageText. Members search worked because we clicked coordinates and queried `input[placeholder]`.

So fix: instead of waitForText('Search tasks'), wait for 'Add task' (FAB) and 'Overdue' section, then use the input placeholder polling. Also fix login: compare identity robustly. After reload, check for a header/avatar label exactly "Alice\nA" or use the avatar text. Simpler: always logout+login as Alice (logout works when logged in; if not, handle). Or determine current user via DOM: header avatar aria-label/text "Bob\nB". Use evaluate to read the top-right avatar tappable text; if not Alice ÔåÆ logout.

Actually simplest: read `document.body.innerText` first line after "Notifications": shows "Bob B". Use regex `/\b(Alice|Bob|Carol|Bruno|admin)\b/`? Names may appear in task rows. Better: the avatar semantics at top has text "Bob\nB". Query semantics nodes with y<60 and x>900 (avatar button) ÔåÆ text. Use the existing avatar finder in logout; adapt to read its text:

```js
const who = await evaluate(send, `(() => {
  for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('flt-semantics[flt-tappable]')) {
    const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
    if (r.y < 60 && r.x > 900 && r.width >= 48) return el.textContent.trim() || el.getAttribute('aria-label');
  }
  return null;
})()`);
```
Then `if (!who || !who.startsWith('Alice')) { await logout(); await login(...); }` but if not logged in, no avatar ÔåÆ login directly.

Do:
```js
const who = ...;
if (!who) { await login('alice...'); } else if (!who.startsWith('Alice')) { await logout(); await login(...); }
```

This is robust against stale E15 state (Bob).

Then update wait:
- After click Planner: `await waitForText('Add task', 20000);` (FAB text)
- Then search input polling when needed.

Also note body shows sections "Overdue/Upcoming/No due date/Completed" ÔÇö good.

Now, about test semantics of the checkbox: need dump. Let me first fix login and wait, then run the exploration part (it dumps nodes after create/search).

Modify e16.

